# JS Code Quality (Awesome-adapted · SPFx scripts)

Defers to `.cursorrules`, `anti-overengineering`, `anti-sycophancy`, `security-appsec`. No React/TS framework scaffolding.

## Mindsets
- Simplicity · readability · maintainability over premature micro-opts
- Testability when logic is non-trivial
- Less code = less debt

## Guidelines
- Early returns over deep nesting
- Descriptive names; event handlers `handle*` (e.g. `handleClick`)
- Prefer clear constants / small pure helpers over sprawling functions
- Prefer immutable/functional style when it stays readable
- DRY only when duplication is real and stable — do not invent shared layers early
- **Minimal diffs** — touch only task-related sections; do not clean unrelated code or rewrite comments

## Comments
- WHY only (non-obvious intent) — no “comment every function”, no restated-code comments
- Prefer JSDoc only for non-obvious public helpers in shared JS

## Bugs found while editing
- If out-of-scope bug: short `TODO:` note OR report in reply — do not drive-by fix unless asked

## Reject
- Importing new libraries without need/approval
- Converting vanilla game/page JS into React/Next/Svelte
- `eval` / unsafe `innerHTML` with user data (see `security-appsec`)
